> My opa applications have a process name SYS$PRGO.$...
> which is not to helpful.
> How do I give them names that mean something to me?

Try the following:

PROC rename:
  local nm$(10),mypid%
  nm$="Hello"
  mypid%=call($88) rem ProcId
  call($c88,mypid%,0,0,0,addr(nm$)+1) rem ProcRename
  busy "Hello"
  get
ENDP

Note: the DI parameter to ProcRename has to point to a C-style ZTS, which 
has to be from 1 to 8 bytes long (not counting the trailing zero).

Take care with your use of ProcRename; if you rename processes other than 
your own, strange effects can ensue!

Regards, DavidW

